 "phrases": [
  "“Therefore the | *government of sages",
  "empties the *mind | and fills the middle,",
  "weakens the | *ambition",
  "and strengthens | the *bones,",
  "always keeping | the people",
  "*innocent | and passionless.”",
  "Can you | *imagine",
  "if we had *sages | running the government",
  "instead of the | *clown show",
  "that we have | of these *politicians?",
  "They wouldn't be | all full of *cleverness.",
  "They wouldn't be | all full of, ~you ~know,",
  "“Oh, we're going to | use this *psyop.",
  "Oh, we're going to use | this *manipulation",
  "of the voter.",
  "Oh, we're going to | *scare them with this.",
  "We're going to | *entice them with this.",
  "We're going to scare | the *hell out of them",
  "that the | *opposing party",
  "is going to | *destroy the country.”",
  "All of this | *non-sage-like behavior,",
  "because when | you do that,",
  "you *hurt | your own people.",
  "And that's | what's *happening.",
  "We've hurt | our *own people.",
  "Our *government | is hurting us",
  "by incessant | *lying",
  "and psychological | *operations",
  "that are designed | to inculcate",
  "*fear or hatred | or worse.",
  "It “weakens | the *ambition",
  "and strengthens | the *bones.”",
  "~So If your country | is just full of",
  "*ambitious people,",
  "there's *nobody | to run anything",
  "because everybody's | too busy",
  "trying to figure out | a way to *get ahead.",
  "So ideally, | you'd want government",
  "where people | were *not ambitious.",
  "They didn't | go in there",
  "to *compete | with each other",
  "as to who | could get",
  "the highest | *net worth",
  "or *position.",
  "“Always keeping | the people",
  "*innocent | and passionless,”",
  "which is kind of | the *opposite",
  "of what we're | doing now.",
  "What we're | doing now",
  "is making the people | *afraid and angry",
  "and putting | each other",
  "at each other's | *throats,",
  "which is | *ridiculous.",
  "You don't want | to *foment emotion",
  "in your people.",
  "You want them | to be *chill.",
  "You want them | to *live their lives.",
  "That's the whole | *function of government,",
  "is to create | an environment",
  "where people | can *flourish",
  "and do | their *work",
  "and *contribute",
  "and take | what they *need.",
  "So we're a | *long way from that.",
  "“It makes | the *sophisticated",
  "not dare | to *contrive.",
  "Action being | without *contrivance,",
  "nothing | is *disordered.”",
  "So in a situation | like this",
  "where *benevolence | actually rules",
  "in the land,",
  "where there's | actually *goodwill,",
  "where there's actually | *integrity and good faith",
  "without | the *extremes,",
  "then the | *sophisticated,",
  "clever people,",
  "they don't dare | to *contrive",
  "because they know | that they're going",
  "to get | *seen through.",
  "This is a | *pillar of Taoism,",
  "and that is to act | without *contrivance.",
  "Just be | *straightforward,",
  "direct."
 ],
